  "id": "COMPOUND:42989 - PROTEIN:5003",
  "verbalization": "Cis-parthenolid-9-one is implicated in the biological pathway leading to ME-180 through a series of molecular interactions involving Gamma-secretase. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including Cis-parthenolid-9-one, which in turn is linked to Ganoderic Acid K and Echinone, all of which ultimately target ME-180. The evidence suggests that Cis-parthenolid-9-one may exert its biological effects by modulating Gamma-secretase activity, which is a key enzyme in the processing of amyloid precursor protein and has been implicated in various pathological processes. The presence of multiple pathways converging on ME-180 through different targets highlights the potential for Cis-parthenolid-9-one to influence cellular processes via this enzyme, possibly through a common mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Gamma-secretase in the context of the drug's biological activity, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
